BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment. The interdisciplinary\, open and collaborative platform fosters 
 creative exchange among artists\, scientists\, writers and other professio
 nals\, with residents initiating participatory local activities that conne
 ct them with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activities\,
  sharing sessions\, media promotion and exhibition opportunities. CYCLES: 
 Spring 2028 (April to June) and Autumn 2028 (July to October)\, each appro
 ximately eight weeks. WHAT YOU GET (International Residency Fellowship\, f
 ully funded): private studio and accommodation\, round-trip economy airfar
 e or second-class train within a set budget\, a production grant of RMB 10
 \,000 per person or team for materials and production (excluding living ex
 penses)\, community engagement and cultural experiences\, media promotion 
 and networking. ELIGIBILITY: multidisciplinary creators worldwide\, includ
 ing visual and performing artists\, musicians\, filmmakers\, architects\, 
 curators\, designers and creatives with interdisciplinary backgrounds brid
 ging art\, business and culture. APPLICATION: free\; submit a photo\, port
 folio\, CV and project proposal in English and Chinese to a4residency@a4am
 .cn\, with the subject line specifying the programme tier and preferred cy
 cle. DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 for the 2028 full-year recruitment. A para
 llel self-funded light track exists\; this listing covers the funded fello
 wship only.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLoca
 tion: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwi
 de.\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, ro
 und-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\
 , and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and 
 production (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: App
 roximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (Ju
 ly to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residency
 artcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-fund-enter-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Fund: ENTER 2026 (exploratory cross-border
  collaboration)
DESCRIPTION:ENTER is the first programme in the Nordic Culture Fund's new p
 ortfolio\, designed to support ambitious ideas that need collaboration to 
 be explored and tested in practice. It offers space to experiment\, learn 
 as you go and test new directions through encounters across disciplines an
 d perspectives\, rather than funding finished productions. WHO CAN APPLY: 
 individuals\, groups\, organisations\, institutions\, associations and com
 panies\, from arts and culture or other sectors\, as long as arts and cult
 ure are central to the initiative. Initiatives need clear Nordic anchoring
  (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\; applicants and pa
 rtners may be based anywhere\, and multiple applications for different ini
 tiatives are permitted. FUNDING: up to DKK 50\,000\, plus up to DKK 25\,00
 0 in accessibility support\, with no co-funding requirement. WHAT IT DOES 
 NOT SUPPORT: education or study visits\, conference or festival participat
 ion\, tours or travelling exhibitions\, productions or publications\, orga
 nisational running costs\, or construction and equipment purchases. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted electronically through the Fund's portal in Danish\, Norw
 egian\, Swedish\, Finnish or English\; no attachments are allowed\, so eve
 rything must fit in the form. Decisions come within five weeks of the dead
 line. The autumn 2026 window runs 14 September to 16 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Nordic Culture Fund\nLocation: Nordic region and beyond. Initiat
 ives must have clear Nordic anchoring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-bor
 der collaboration\, but applicants and partners may be based anywhere.\nAw
 ard: Up to DKK 50\,000 (roughly EUR 6\,700)\, plus up to DKK 25\,000 in ad
 ditional accessibility support for logistics and access needs\, for a maxi
 mum total of DKK 75\,000. No co-funding required. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Projects may run up to one year from the stated start date\, genera
 lly non-extendable.\n\nMore: https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-prog
 rammes/give-ambitious-ideas-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-programmes/give-ambitious-idea
 s-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Nordic region and beyond. Initiatives must have clear Nordic ancho
 ring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\, but applicant
 s and partners may be based anywhere.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-festival-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, opens its fifth call: 50 residencies for 50 emerging artists (indi
 viduals\, groups or collectives) hosted by partnerships of around 150 fest
 ivals\, each led by one leading festival with a minimum of two partner fes
 tivals from different eligible countries. TWO CATEGORIES: EFFEA Discovery\
 , 40 grants of EUR 8\,000 for artists at the early stages of their careers
  with strong potential to break through internationally\; and EFFEA Spring
 board\, 10 grants of EUR 15\,000 for artists already established in their 
 own country and ready to develop their careers internationally. A Discover
 y residency includes a work-in-progress presentation at the leading festiv
 al\, a workshop with programmers from each partner festival\, a short film
  about the residency\, and participation in the EFFEA Intake and Outtake S
 eminars\; a Springboard residency includes at least three presentations of
  the production result (leading festival plus each partner festival) and a
  live masterclass by the artist in at least three countries. DISCIPLINES: 
 architecture\, ballet\, contemporary dance\, circus\, design and applied a
 rts\, digital arts\, film\, folklore and folk arts\, heritage\, interdisci
 plinary\, literature\, music\, opera\, street art\, theatre\, photography 
 and video\, puppetry\, sculpture\, painting. WHO APPLIES: the leading fest
 ival submits the application online via the EFFEA website and proposes the
  artists\; festivals must be registered on FestivalFinder.eu and have held
  at least one edition. Artists may be of any age and must have nationality
  or legal residence in an eligible country. Emerging is defined by novelty
  to programmers and audiences\, not by age. FINANCES: minimum 80 percent o
 f the grant goes to artist costs\; own contributions of EUR 1\,000 (Discov
 ery) or EUR 2\,000 (Springboard) are deducted from the grant\; in-kind cos
 ts are capped at 10 percent. TIMELINE: evaluation in November 2026\, resul
 ts by email in December 2026\, residencies between 1 January and 31 Decemb
 er 2027 (Intake Seminar 26 January 2027\, Outtake Seminar 21 September 202
 7). Deadline 3 November 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: European Festi
 vals Association (EFA)\nLocation: Residencies hosted by festival partnersh
 ips of at least three festivals from three eligible countries (most of Eur
 ope plus Tunisia and Ukraine). Leading festivals and artists must be based
  in an eligible country\; festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\
 , Turkey and the UK may join as partner festivals only\, and artists from 
 those countries may also be proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing th
 e artists\; artists cannot apply directly.\nAward: 50 residency grants: 40
  Discovery grants of EUR 8\,000 (for artists at an early career stage) and
  10 Springboard grants of EUR 15\,000 (for artists established at home and
  ready to break through internationally). A minimum of 80 percent of the g
 rant must cover costs incurred by the artists (fees\, travel\, accommodati
 on\, subsistence). An own contribution of EUR 1\,000 (Discovery) or EUR 2\
 ,000 (Springboard) is deducted from the paid grant. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Residencies implemented between 1 January and 31 December 2027\, 
 co-produced by one leading festival and at least two partner festivals\n\n
 More: https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residencies hosted by festival partnerships of at least three fest
 ivals from three eligible countries (most of Europe plus Tunisia and Ukrai
 ne). Leading festivals and artists must be based in an eligible country\; 
 festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\, Turkey and the UK may jo
 in as partner festivals only\, and artists from those countries may also b
 e proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the artists\; artists cannot
  apply directly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heavens-hospital-next-nature-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Deadline: Next Nature: Heaven's Hospital Open Call (commissions on 
 the future of care)
DESCRIPTION:Heaven's Hospital\, a research and presentation platform and ex
 hibition at the Next Nature Museum\, invites designers\, artists\, archite
 cts\, filmmakers\, writers\, technologists\, game developers\, researchers
 \, scientists\, care professionals and other creative makers to develop ne
 w perspectives on the future of care. Starting from the question of how ca
 re environments can transform from repair factories into sensory ecosystem
 s\, the open call The Dreamed-Up Care seeks fresh ideas rather than ready-
 made solutions: speculative designs\, artistic research\, future scenarios
 \, prototypes\, new applications of AI\, architecture\, digital systems\, 
 rituals\, films\, installations\, services and new forms of collaboration.
  TWELVE CARE ISSUES frame the call\, including the shift from illness to h
 ealth\, the hospital as machine\, staff shortages\, AI changing the role o
 f the doctor\, the patient as data producer\, chronic conditions\, mental 
 health\, the missing human experience in hospitals\, care inequality\, cli
 mate and care\, fragmentation of treatment\, and the medicalisation of bir
 th\, old age and dying. WHAT THEY WANT: projects exploring the future of h
 ealthcare through artistic research\, speculative design or technological 
 innovation that actively engage the public (installations\, interactive en
 vironments\, spatial interventions\, digital experiences\, games\, perform
 ances or other participatory forms)\, and cross-disciplinary work combinin
 g design with AI\, robotics\, immersive media\, biotechnology\, synthetic 
 biology\, architecture\, food design\, sound design\, data science\, ecolo
 gy or philosophy. SUPPORT: three selected projects each receive EUR 15\,00
 0 to develop a first prototype or artistic intervention\, become Heaven's 
 Hospital Fellows\, contribute to the ongoing research programme and may be
  publicly presented in the Next Nature Museum. Proposals must be feasible 
 within the available time and budget while remaining ambitious and experim
 ental. WHO CAN APPLY: individuals or collectives. HOW TO APPLY: one propos
 al per participant via the online application portal\, consisting of the c
 ompleted application form\, a CV and a portfolio of maximum 10 pages or sl
 ides\; PDF only\, maximum 4 MB per file\, in English or Dutch. SELECTION C
 RITERIA: originality and imagination\, relevance to the future of healthca
 re\, artistic and design quality\, innovative use of technology\, public e
 ngagement\, feasibility\, and potential contribution to the research progr
 amme. TIMELINE: deadline 20 October 2026\; jury meets November 2026\; sele
 cted participants announced December 2026\; research\, development and pro
 totype production through 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Heaven's Hospital / Next 
 Nature Museum\nLocation: Next Nature Museum\, Eindhoven\, the Netherlands.
  Open internationally\; applications in English or Dutch.\nAward: Three se
 lected projects each receive a budget of EUR 15\,000 for the development o
 f a first prototype or artistic intervention. Selected participants become
  Heaven's Hospital Fellows and join an international network of designers\
 , researchers\, care professionals and artists. No application fee stated.
 \nDuration: Research\, development and prototype production during 2027\, 
 with presentation within the Heaven's Hospital exhibition at the Next Natu
 re Museum.\n\nMore: https://nextnature.org/en/opencall?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nextnature.org/en/opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Next Nature Museum\, Eindhoven\, the Netherlands. Open internation
 ally\; applications in English or Dutch.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pulitzer-center-global-south-civil-society-microgrants-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pulitzer Center: Global South Civil Society Microgrants 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Pulitzer Center funds civil society in the Global South to 
 build civic engagement projects around Pulitzer Center-supported journalis
 m: grassroots collectives\, community-led movements\, ARTISTS and civic co
 alitions taking published reporting to the communities it concerns. This g
 rant cycle is restricted to the Center's Climate and Environment topics: R
 AINFOREST (drivers of rainforest degradation\, the role of global markets\
 , finance and policy\, centring the rights and roles of Indigenous peoples
 )\, OCEAN (degradation of marine environments\, ocean health and the clima
 te crisis\, ocean governance\, science-backed and community-led solutions)
 \, and CLIMATE AND LABOR (the intersection of climate and labour\, includi
 ng gender\, livelihoods\, adaptation and community resilience). WHAT COUNT
 S AS A PROJECT: community engagement and organising that connects reportin
 g with audiences\; creative expressions\, explicitly including digital cam
 paigns\, public performances and creative publication formats\; public dia
 logues bringing together affected communities\, journalists\, decision-mak
 ers and academia\; and other innovative uses of the reporting that build o
 n local cultural practices. Every project must use at least one published 
 Pulitzer Center-supported reporting project meaningfully\, or involve a Pu
 litzer Center-supported journalist centrally\, and must name a clear targe
 t audience. OUT OF SCOPE: journalism and reporting projects themselves (th
 ose go to the Center's reporting grants)\, anything not built on Pulitzer 
 Center-supported reporting\, direct advocacy or lobbying\, campaigns endor
 sing political candidates or parties\, and for-profit projects. WHO CAN AP
 PLY: grassroots organisations\, community educators\, civil society organi
 sations and coalitions\, youth movements and other groups working at the i
 ntersection of journalism\, civic rights and active citizenship\, with pas
 t experience running civic engagement activities in the Global South\, pro
 ven experience on the named topics\, and the operational capacity to manag
 e a microgrant from an international organisation. APPLICATION: a project 
 description of no more than 400 words\, the target audience and desired im
 pact\, your methodology\, a timeline and budget\, the lead applicant's CV 
 with a letter of recommendation\, and\, where activities involve Indigenou
 s peoples or traditional communities\, a signed or recorded statement of c
 onsent from a community member. Applications are accepted in English\, Spa
 nish\, Portuguese\, French and Indonesian through Submittable. TIMELINE: a
 pplications 15 August to 6 September 2026\, selection announced mid-Septem
 ber 2026\, onboarding October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pulitzer Center\nLoca
 tion: Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and South
 east Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. Ci
 vil Society Microgrant instead.\nAward: USD 2\,000 to USD 4\,000 per proje
 ct. Applicants name the amount requested and submit a draft budget. Funds 
 are transferred to the partner after the agreement is signed\; partners fi
 le a financial narrative and outcomes report at the end but are NOT requir
 ed to collect detailed receipts. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to six 
 months of implementation\, October 2026 to March 2027\, with a virtual che
 ck-in in December 2026 and closure in early March 2027.\n\nMore: https://p
 ulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/global-south-
 civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://pulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/g
 lobal-south-civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and Sou
 theast Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. 
 Civil Society Microgrant instead.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:guggenheim-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Guggenheim Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Guggenheim Fellowship is awarded to mid-career individuals 
 who have already demonstrated exceptional capacity for productive scholars
 hip or exceptional creative ability in the arts\, giving them six to twelv
 e months of funded time to work with as much creative freedom as possible.
  Around 175 to 200 fellows are chosen each year from a field of several th
 ousand applicants (a success rate of roughly five percent)\, across more t
 han 50 fields spanning the creative arts\, the humanities\, the natural sc
 iences and the social sciences\, including architecture\, film\, music\, p
 hotography\, fine arts\, computer science and interdisciplinary work. ELIG
 IBILITY: citizens and permanent residents of the United States and Canada\
 ; applicants must be mid-career with a significant record of published or 
 exhibited work\, and current students and previous Guggenheim Fellows are 
 not eligible. APPLICATION: through the Foundation's own portal\, which ope
 ns in late summer 2026\, so check the site if it is not yet live. The appl
 ication deadline is 15 September 2026 with no late submissions accepted\; 
 work samples are due 29 September 2026 and reference letters 13 October 20
 26. Results are announced in late April 2027. No fee.\n\nOrganisation: Joh
 n Simon Guggenheim Memorial Foundation\nLocation: Anywhere\; the fellowshi
 p funds the fellow's own work rather than residence at a host institution.
  Open to citizens and permanent residents of the United States and Canada.
 \nAward: Variable cash grant sized to the applicant's proposed budget and 
 needs\; the Foundation does not publish a fixed figure or range\, and rece
 nt awards have typically run into the tens of thousands of US dollars. Rou
 ghly 175 to 200 fellowships are awarded each year across more than 50 fiel
 ds. The Foundation charges no application fee and has no affiliated applic
 ation consultants.\nDuration: Six to twelve months of supported work\n\nMo
 re: https://www.gf.org/program/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.gf.org/program/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Anywhere\; the fellowship funds the fellow's own work rather than 
 residence at a host institution. Open to citizens and permanent residents 
 of the United States and Canada.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:red-quincho-beca-constelaciones-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: Red Quincho: Beca Constelaciones 2026 (4th Edition)
DESCRIPTION:Beca Constelaciones is Red Quincho's mobility and production gr
 ant for artists\, curators and researchers doing territory-based work\, no
 w in its fourth edition. Each recipient spends one month in residence\, sp
 lit into two 15-day placements at different member spaces across Argentina
 \, pairing an urban and a rural context. The grant covers mobility\, livin
 g costs and production\, with lodging provided. Backed by Fundacion Willia
 ms\, CCEBA and Fundacion Santander through the CABA Mecenazgo scheme. ELIG
 IBILITY IS RESTRICTED: of the 15 grants\, 13 are for people resident in Ar
 gentina and 2 are for people currently living in Spain. Artists\, curators
  and researchers apply through separate forms\; Spanish-based candidates f
 ace an additional jury evaluation. Deadline 9 August 2026 at 23:59 Argenti
 na time.\n\nOrganisation: Red Quincho\nLocation: Rotating urban and rural 
 Red Quincho spaces across Argentina\; residency runs September to December
  2026.\nAward: ARS 1\,000\,000 (around USD 690) per grant toward mobility\
 , living costs and production\, plus one month of lodging. 15 grants avail
 able. No application fee.\nDuration: One-month residency split into two 15
 -day placements at different spaces.\n\nMore: https://redquincho.ar/beca-c
 onstelaciones-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://redquincho.ar/beca-constelaciones-2026/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotating urban and rural Red Quincho spaces across Argentina\; res
 idency runs September to December 2026.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kone-foundation-annual-grant-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kone Foundation: Annual Grant Call (2026)
DESCRIPTION:Kone Foundation is Finland's major private funder for academic 
 research in the humanities\, social sciences and environmental sciences\, 
 for professional artistic work across all disciplines\, and specifically f
 or multidisciplinary projects combining scholarly and artistic approaches\
 , which is where digital culture\, media arts and artistic research propos
 als land. Individuals\, working groups and legal entities with a Finnish b
 usiness ID may apply\, and artistic groups and organisations can receive u
 p to EUR 250\,000. The Finland connection is the binding constraint: a non
 -Finnish applicant needs a Finnish institutional affiliation\, Finland res
 idence\, or the work must happen in Finland\, though international collabo
 rators can join a group freely once one member is a Finnish citizen or Fin
 land-based. Psychology\, theology\, law\, business studies without an inte
 rdisciplinary element\, and medical research are not funded\, nor are mast
 er's studies\, continuing education\, building renovation\, standalone equ
 ipment purchases or hobby activity. The annual call runs 1 to 15 September
  each year\, closing 15 September 2026 at 16:00 EEST\, with decisions anno
 unced in November and December. TIMING: funding is never retroactive and p
 rojects must begin in January or later\, so a September 2026 application f
 unds work starting January 2027 at the earliest. FLAG: Kone frames its fun
 ding around artistic work and research projects rather than festival or ev
 ent hosting as such\, so an event-led application needs to be framed as an
  artistic or research project.\n\nOrganisation: Kone Foundation / Koneen S
 aatio (Finland)\nLocation: Finland. Work may be carried out abroad by Finn
 ish citizens. Projects must have a connection to Finland.\nAward: Artistic
  groups and organisations up to EUR 250\,000\; research groups typically E
 UR 200\,000 to 500\,000. Minimum project duration six months for individua
 l applicants and one month for groups\; maximum four consecutive years for
  the same project. No co-financing requirement stated. No application fee.
  No retroactive funding.\nDuration: One month to four years\; projects mus
 t start in January or later.\n\nMore: https://koneensaatio.fi/en/grants/gr
 antapplicants/criteria-for-applying/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://koneensaatio.fi/en/grants/grantapplicants/criteria-for-applying
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Finland. Work may be carried out abroad by Finnish citizens. Proje
 cts must have a connection to Finland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:simons-foundation-open-interval-turbulence-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Interval: An Artist-Scientist Exploration of Turbule
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Open Interval is a Simons Foundation program that supports trio
 s consisting of an artist\, a scientist\, and a representative from a 501(
 c)(3) arts organization to collaborate around a shared scientific theme. T
 he current cycle centers on the theme of turbulence\, a phenomenon at the 
 edge of chaos and beauty. Awarded trios receive USD 30\,000 to support a s
 ustained period of thought partnership and exploration rather than the pro
 duction of finished works or exhibitions. The program runs from April to D
 ecember 2027 with a touchstone meeting in May 2027 and possible cohort con
 venings. Trio members must be regionally co-located anywhere in the United
  States so they can collaborate in person. The scientist should hold a Ph.
 D. and be conducting basic research\, with priority given to fields such a
 s astrophysics\, neuroscience\, quantum physics\, biology\, or mathematics
 . The application portal opens September 9\, 2026\, and all three trio mem
 bers must submit for the application to be complete.\n\nOrganisation: Simo
 ns Foundation\nLocation: United States (trio must be regionally co-located
 )\nAward: USD 30\,000 per awarded trio\nDuration: April to December 2027 (
 several months of collaboration)\n\nMore: https://www.simonsfoundation.org
 /2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-an-artist-scientist-exploration-of-t
 urbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-a
 n-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (trio must be regionally co-located)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:british-council-connections-through-culture-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:Deadline: Connections Through Culture Grants 2026 (British Council)
DESCRIPTION:Connections Through Culture (CTC) grants are designed to enable
  meaningful partnerships\, cross-cultural exchange and long-term collabora
 tion between the UK and participating countries. In 2026\, CTC incorporate
 s the grants programmes formerly known as Biennials Connect (Visual Arts) 
 and Architecture\, Design and Fashion Biennials and Festivals Grants\, and
  serves as the British Council's major Arts grants programme for 2026 (in 
 place of International Collaboration Grants). It offers grants of between 
 GBP 5\,000 and GBP 15\,000 to support creative practitioners\, cultural pr
 ofessionals\, artists\, organisations\, festivals\, biennials\, hubs and c
 ollectives to develop and deliver collaborative projects across a wide ran
 ge of themes and art forms\, including applied arts\, architecture\, curat
 ing\, dance\, design\, digital\, drawing\, education\, fashion\, film\, in
 stallation\, interdisciplinary work\, painting\, performance\, photography
 \, printmaking\, public art\, research\, sculpture\, social practice\, sou
 nd art\, textiles\, video\, visual arts and writing. ELIGIBILITY: applicat
 ions must involve collaboration between at least one UK-based partner and 
 at least one partner based in an eligible participating country\; each par
 tner must be legally based in the country they are applying from at the ti
 me of application and throughout the project activity period. PARTICIPATIN
 G COUNTRIES: Albania\, Argentina\, Australia\, Bangladesh\, Bosnia and Her
 zegovina\, Colombia\, Mainland China\, Egypt\, Indonesia\, Kazakhstan\, Ke
 nya\, Kosovo\, Lebanon\, Malaysia\, Mexico\, Montenegro\, New Zealand\, Ni
 geria\, North Macedonia\, Pakistan\, Palestine\, Peru\, Philippines\, Saud
 i Arabia\, Serbia\, South Africa\, Tanzania\, Thailand\, Tunisia\, Turkey\
 , United Arab Emirates\, UK\, Ukraine\, Uzbekistan\, Venezuela\, and Vietn
 am. Eligible applicants include artists and creative practitioners\, arts 
 and cultural organisations\, festivals and biennials\, cultural profession
 als\, creative hubs/networks/collectives\, and organisations working acros
 s arts\, culture and the creative sectors. Note: applications involving pr
 ojects organised by or taking place as part of Visual Arts\, Architecture\
 , Design\, Fashion and Craft festivals should be made by the festival or b
 iennial organisation rather than by individual artists\, designers or prac
 titioners. No application fee. Deadline 12 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: B
 ritish Council\nLocation: International collaboration grant. Each applicat
 ion must involve at least one UK-based partner and at least one partner ba
 sed in an eligible participating country\; each partner must be legally ba
 sed in the country they apply from throughout the project.\nAward: Grants 
 of between GBP 5\,000 and GBP 15\,000. Free to apply.\nDuration: Project-b
 ased\; develop and deliver collaborative projects across a range of themes
  and art forms.\n\nMore: https://arts.britishcouncil.org/connections-throu
 gh-culture?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.britishcouncil.org/connections-through-culture?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International collaboration grant. Each application must involve a
 t least one UK-based partner and at least one partner based in an eligible
  participating country\; each partner must be legally based in the country
  they apply from throughout the project.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-grounding-the-cloud-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Grounding the Cloud 2026
DESCRIPTION:Open call from the Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfon
 ds) for projects within digital culture that provide insight into and redu
 ce the ecological impact of digital technology. Data storage in the cloud\
 , generative AI chatbots and other everyday digital habits carry major eco
 logical consequences: the energy consumption of data centres\, the raw mat
 erials used for hardware\, and ever-growing e-waste. The Fund encourages p
 rojects that make the ecological (and therefore also social) impact of dig
 ital technologies and data consumption tangible\, question it\, and put al
 ternative working methods into practice\, around topics such as regenerati
 ve culture\, degrowth\, low-tech\, the reuse of obsolete hardware\, and re
 sponsibility for the technologies we use within digital culture. Applicati
 ons may concern new projects or the reinterpretation or further developmen
 t of existing initiatives that show scope for more depth or a changed appr
 oach. Collaborations in which designers\, makers or researchers engage wit
 h sustainability from an intersectional perspective are explicitly encoura
 ged. The grant may be used for artistic and substantive development\, rese
 arch\, collaboration\, knowledge sharing\, presentation and documentation.
  ELIGIBILITY: individual makers\, designers\, researchers or collectives w
 orking on alternative ways of handling digital technology\, registered wit
 h a Chamber of Commerce within the Kingdom of the Netherlands. Grant award
 s a maximum of EUR 30\,000\; maximum project duration one year. This call 
 is open from 17 August 2026\, 15:00 CEST until 14 September 2026\, 16:00 C
 EST. No application fee. Questions: digitalecultuur@stimuleringsfonds.nl.\
 n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK
 ) registration within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: Maximum EUR 
 30\,000 per grant. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; maximum 
 project duration one year.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gr
 ants/open-call-grounding-the-cloud?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-grounding-the-clou
 d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration
  within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-immerse-interact-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds + Film Fund: Immerse\\Interact 2026 (se
 cond round)
DESCRIPTION:Immerse\\Interact is a joint grant scheme of the Stimuleringsfo
 nds Creatieve Industrie and the Netherlands Film Fund for immersive and in
 teractive media projects (VR\, MR\, AR and other interactive storytelling)
 . It supports artistic projects with a supporting cinematic component\, in
  which fiction or non-fiction storytelling in relation to interactive (web
 -based/mobile) or immersive technologies (XR\, room-scale projections) is 
 central. It funds both development and realisation. Development support is
  EUR 15\,000 for individual makers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching\, cappe
 d at EUR 20\,000 total) or EUR 25\,000 for producers (plus up to EUR 5\,00
 0 coaching)\; the coaching contribution requires a motivation from both ap
 plicant and coach plus the coach's CV\, and the development phase must res
 ult in a usable prototype. A maximum of six development contributions are 
 awarded per round\, to keep the development and realisation budgets in bal
 ance. Realisation support is up to EUR 35\,000 for individual makers or up
  to EUR 125\,000 for producers (the Fund covers a maximum of 85 percent of
  the production budget)\; note that at realisation stage the producer may 
 not also be the director\, screenwriter or designer. A separate Presentati
 on Procedure offers presentation grants for projects previously supported 
 by Immerse\\Interact after 1 January 2022. EUR 600\,000 is available per F
 und in 2026. Open to professional makers\, collectives and producers with 
 a demonstrable track record in immersive or interactive media\; applicants
  must be registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK). The second 2
 026 round runs 24 June to 25 August 2026 (opens 24 June 15:00\, closes 25 
 August 16:00 CEST). No application fee. Questions: immerseinteract@stimule
 ringsfonds.nl.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie and 
 the Netherlands Film Fund\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber o
 f Commerce (KvK) registration.\nAward: Development: EUR 15\,000 for indivi
 dual makers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching\, max EUR 20\,000) or EUR 25\,
 000 for producers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching). Realisation: up to EUR
  35\,000 for individual makers or up to EUR 125\,000 for producers (Fund c
 overs max 85 percent). No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, deve
 lopment and realisation phases.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/
 en/grants/immerse-interact-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/immerse-interact-grant-schem
 e?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration
 .
