UID:make-a-thek-mobility-knowledge-exchange-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: make-a-thek: Mobility Scheme & Knowledge Exchange Program
 me (Europe + pilot countries)
DESCRIPTION:make-a-thek\, a Horizon Europe project (grant No. 101177660) co
 ordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, connects creative spaces\, public
  libraries and makers across Europe and beyond to share skills in circular
  fashion\, traditional crafts and technology. Its open call runs two track
 s. MOBILITY SCHEME (Track A): experienced practitioners (make-a-thek Exper
 ts) travel to an EU pilot location (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Budapes
 t\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv or Zaporizhzhia) t
 o deliver a workshop\, talk or hands-on training\, with a EUR 1\,000 stipe
 nd to support expenses. KNOWLEDGE EXCHANGE PROGRAMME (Track B): learners\,
  practitioners\, makers\, craftspeople and librarians travel to a 2-day in
 -person group meet-up (Cohort 1 in Barcelona between end of November and s
 tart of December 2026\; Cohort 2 in Berlin in May 2027)\, then organise a 
 local knowledge-sharing activity\, with a EUR 850 stipend. Up to 12 partic
 ipants per track annually. ELIGIBILITY: legal residents of EU member state
 s\, Horizon Europe associated countries\, or the international pilot count
 ries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, the Philippines and Chile\; propos
 als must align with at least one focus area: Circular Fashion\, Digitising
  Traditional Crafts\, or Open Technologies. HOW TO APPLY: via the Typeform
  linked from the open call page. The early-bird round closed 15 September 
 2026\; late applications are accepted until 1 December 2026\, and the next
  call runs 1 February to 31 March 2027. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: make-a-thek (coordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, funded b
 y Horizon Europe)\nLocation: Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barc
 elona\, Berlin\, Budapest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\,
  Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)\; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) an
 d Berlin (May 2027). Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon
  Europe associated countries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Afric
 a\, Indonesia\, Philippines and Chile.\nAward: Mobility Scheme: EUR 1\,000
  flat stipend for experienced practitioners. Knowledge Exchange Programme:
  EUR 850 flat stipend. Up to 12 participants per track annually. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Short-term mobility: single events\, workshops or 2-
 day group meet-ups (Barcelona between end of November and start of Decembe
 r 2026\; Berlin in May 2027).\n\nMore: https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Buda
 pest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)
 \; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). 
 Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon Europe associated co
 untries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, Phili
 ppines and Chile.
END:VEVENT
