DESCRIPTION:Online incubator from Swiss foundation Unearthodox (formerly th
 e Luc Hoffmann Institute) for innovators with early-stage ideas at the int
 ersection of environmental and societal challenges\, aimed at work that ta
 ckles root causes in the relationship between people\, society and nature 
 rather than symptoms: climate\, biodiversity\, habitat loss\, regeneration
  and environmental justice among them. WHAT YOU GET: a CHF 10\,000 grant p
 lus 10 months of cohort-based incubation (March to December 2027) with coa
 ching\, expert and peer support\, and access to a global community of syst
 ems innovators. ELIGIBILITY: over 18\, idea already in motion through rese
 arch\, testing\, piloting or community engagement\; applications in Englis
 h\; participation fully online with sessions planned for UTC-6 to UTC+6. S
 ELECTION CRITERIA: systems orientation (25 percent)\, nature-society visio
 n (25 percent)\, boundary-pushing (25 percent)\, transformational intent (
 15 percent)\, edge-walking (10 percent). DEADLINE: 16 November 2026\, 23:5
 9 GMT+1 (window opened 15 September 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Unearthodox\nL
 ocation: Online\; group sessions designed around time zones UTC-6 to UTC+6
 . Open worldwide to applicants over 18\; applications in English.\nAward: 
 CHF 10\,000 grant per selected initiative\, plus a 10-month incubation pro
 gramme with tailored coaching\, expert support\, peer learning\, systems m
 apping and futures-thinking support. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 mon
 ths\, 1 March to 31 December 2027\n\nMore: https://unearthodox.org/2026/09
 /open-call-edges-of-possibility-exploration-co-lab-2027/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
