UID:cerv-2026-citizens-rem@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T130015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270225
SUMMARY:Deadline: EU CERV: European Remembrance 2026-27 (CERV-2026-CITIZENS
 -REM)
DESCRIPTION:The EU's main remembrance funding line\, and emphatically not H
 olocaust-only: the 2026-27 call (covering both years\; there is no separat
 e 2027 call) funds projects across four topics: 1) remembering democratic 
 transitions and the (re)building of democratic institutions\; 2) remembran
 ce of the Holocaust against Jewish people\; 3) remembrance of the Holocaus
 t\, acts of genocide\, war crimes and crimes against humanity\, with prior
 ities on Roma victims and on LGBTIQ+ and other victims\; 4) the legacy of 
 colonialism\, slavery and migration in contemporary multicultural European
  societies. Previous rounds funded exhibitions\, digital archives\, testim
 ony projects\, memorial education and artistic memory work. ELIGIBILITY: l
 ead applicant must be a non-profit legal entity (public or private) or int
 ernational organisation established in an EU Member State or CERV-associat
 ed country\; for-profits only as co-applicants alongside public or non-pro
 fit partners\; each application addresses exactly one topic. TIMELINE: cal
